#
# Counter-example for the native math:ProbabilityOutOfBounds gate: a
# math:ProbabilityValue whose math:quantityValue magnitude carries an EXPLICIT leading
# '+' sign ("+1.5"), a valid xsd:decimal lexical form. The exact-rational reader must
# strip the '+' the same way it strips a leading '-', so the magnitude still parses to
# 3/2 and lies outside the closed unit interval [0, 1] — the native probability gate
# MUST emit math:ProbabilityOutOfBounds (and no other probability failure class). It
# carries a gmeow:hasReferenceFrame so math:ProbabilityValueFramedShape (P3) stays
# SATISFIED, isolating exactly the out-of-bounds range gate.
# Back-reference: math:ProbabilityValue / math:ProbabilityOutOfBounds (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:outOfBoundsSignedProbability a math:ProbabilityValue ;
    math:quantityValue "+1.5" ;
    gmeow:hasReferenceFrame ex:outOfBoundsSignedFrame .

ex:outOfBoundsSignedFrame a gmeow:ReferenceFrame .
<http://example.org/math/outOfBoundsSignedProbability> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasDimension> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dimensionless> .
